course: dictionary
lesson: 4518
title: One word, several meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 1
explain: Many words have more than one meaning, and «heading» is one of them. The sentence around the word tells you which meaning is right, so always read the context before you decide.
explain: «A non-chronological report organises facts by topic, not by time, usually in the present tense with headings.» Here a heading is the title at the top of a part of the writing. It tells you what that part is about, so you can find things fast.
explain: «A girl in Calgary heading for the ice rink puts on her helmet and gloves.» Here heading is the -ing form of head, the verb. She is going towards the rink. Same word family, different job in the sentence.
explain: Use the swap test. Put your meaning into the sentence and check it still makes sense. «A girl in Calgary going towards the ice rink» works, so heading means going towards there in this sentence.
fact: A heading is the title at the top of a page, section or piece of writing that tells you what it is about.
fact: Headings and subheadings organise information and help the reader find things.
fact: Heading is the -ing form of head, so «heading home» means going home.
fact: A heading can also be a direction of travel, given in degrees: a heading of 090 degrees means east.
fact: In football, heading means hitting the ball with your head.
exercise: «A non-chronological report organises facts by topic, not by time, usually in the present tense with headings.» In this sentence, what is a heading? | *The title that tells you what a part of the writing is about | A number of degrees on a map | A tram going towards five people | The top part of a girl's head
exercise: «A girl in Calgary heading for the ice rink puts on her helmet and gloves.» What does heading mean here? | A title at the top of a page | A direction given in degrees | *Going towards | Hitting a ball with your head
exercise: «A report on penguins is sorted by topic, not by time, under headings like "Habitat" and "Diet".» Find and copy one heading. | *Habitat | Penguins | Time | Topic
test: «Every page is built from three languages: HTML says what is on it (headings, pictures, links).» In this sentence, what are headings? | Directions given in degrees | Pictures on the page | *Titles that tell you what is on the page | Ways of hitting a ball
test: «The trolley problem pictures a runaway tram heading for five people.» What does heading mean here? | Written in the present tense | *Moving towards | Hitting with the head | A title at the top of a section
exam: In maths and navigation, «a heading of 090 degrees» means the ship is travelling in which direction? | South | *East | West | North
